    "scientific_conclusion": "No single-frame snapshot reproduces the continuous dual-corridor refinement band shown in Pandey & Kumar Figure 15(b). At early states (State 1-2), error is strictly confined to the primary crack. At mid-states (State 3-4), error shifts to the secondary crack while the primary crack sheds error. At the terminal state (State 5), both cracks are fully degraded and stress error concentrates on pin-hole boundaries. A continuous dual-corridor band covering both primary and secondary trajectories simultaneously originates from a multi-frame trajectory envelope, cumulative historical error, or an explicit trajectory-based sizing field."
